@startuml

title ORE as a relying party: the gateway holds the browser, IAM holds the identity

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor "the person's\nbrowser" as browser
participant "ores.http\n(the gateway)" as gateway
participant "the provider\n(issuer)" as provider
participant "ores.vault" as vault
participant "ores.iam" as iam

browser -> gateway : GET /api/auth/providers
gateway -> iam : the providers this address enables
iam --> gateway : provider codes and names
gateway --> browser : the doors this tenant offers

browser -> gateway : GET /api/auth/external/start?provider=...
gateway -> gateway : state, nonce, and a PKCE verifier it keeps for this attempt
gateway --> browser : 302 to the provider, with code_challenge=S256
browser -> provider : the person consents
provider --> browser : 302 to the exact redirect address, with code and state
browser -> gateway : GET the callback, with code and state

gateway -> gateway : refuse a state it did not mint
gateway -> vault : the client secret the provider row names
vault --> gateway : sealed to the gateway, opened in memory
gateway -> provider : code, the PKCE verifier, and the client secret
provider --> gateway : an ID token and an access token

gateway -> gateway : validate iss, aud, exp, nonce, and the signature by kid
gateway -> iam : sign in as issuer and subject, through a provider
iam -> iam : link found, or a first sign-in that registers through the policy
iam --> gateway : the session, or a refusal with its code
gateway --> browser : the session cookie, under the hardening it already has

@enduml
